From a794545ded000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kepler_compute: stop the native upload bookkeeping leak on PS5

Every native exec_upload currently appends a 24-byte UploadInfo to `uploads`,
but only the legacy launch path consumes and clears that vector. On the PS5
console this was about 2,900 entries per second: a 96 MiB heap block at
13 minutes and 192 MiB at 24 minutes. It is a long-lived reservation and its
vector growth also creates allocator churn at the area-change boundary.

The native path never needs the legacy upload list, so disable that store by
default for PS5_NATIVE. EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_STORE=0 remains an explicit rollback;
other targets retain the old opt-in behavior.

---
 src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/engines/kepler_compute.cpp
@@ -42,7 +42,11 @@ namespace {
 bool NoUploadStore() {
     static const bool no_store = [] {
         const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_NO_UPLOAD_STORE");
+#ifdef PS5_NATIVE
+        return value == nullptr || value[0] == '1';
+#else
         return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+#endif
     }();
     return no_store;
 }
